You may distribute copies or modified versions of the Software for
noncommercial purposes, provided that you include this license and the
applicable copyright and third-party notices, clearly identify your changes,
and do not misrepresent a modified version as the original project.

4. No commercialization of the Software

Without separate written permission from the applicable copyright holder, you
may not sell, rent, sublicense for a fee, or otherwise commercialize the Software
itself, any modified version, or any substantial portion of its source or
executable code as a product or service.

This restriction includes selling source code or packaged applications; paid,
subscription-based, advertising-supported, or otherwise monetized hosted
versions or SaaS; white-label resale; and incorporating the Software or
substantial portions of it into a commercial product or service. Offering a
free tier does not exempt such a commercial product or service.

Using the Software internally to create commercial Outputs, or showing it while
presenting your work, is not by itself commercialization of the Software.
Charging for access to the Software or its functionality is different from
charging for the works you create with it, and is not permitted under this license.

